      "name": "validate_schema",
      "arguments": {
        "document": "{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"difficultyLevel\",\"route\",\"estimatedLatency\",\"provider\"],\"properties\":{\"difficultyLevel\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"easy\",\"medium\",\"hard\",\"expert\"]},\"route\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1},\"estimatedLatency\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"minimum\":0},\"provider\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"local\",\"remote\"]},\"fallback\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "apply_patch",
      "arguments": {
        "diff": "--- router.ts\n+++ router.ts\n@@ -1,3 +1,42 @@\n+export interface LatencyProfile {\n+  meanMs: number;\n+  p95Ms: number;\n+  p99Ms: number;\n+}\n+\n+export interface RouteDecision {\n+  provider: 'local' | 'remote';\n+  reason: string;\n+  expectedLatencyMs: number;\n+}\n+\n export function createRouter(config: RouterConfig): Router {\n   return new RouterImpl(config);\n }\n+\n+export function compareLatencyProfiles(local: LatencyProfile, remote: LatencyProfile): 'local' | 'remote' {\n+  if (local.p95Ms < remote.p95Ms) return 'local';\n+  if (remote.p95Ms < local.p95Ms) return 'remote';\n+  if (local.meanMs < remote.meanMs) return 'local';\n+  return 'remote';\n+}\n+\n+export function decideDifficultyRoute(\n+  difficulty: 'easy' | 'medium' | 'hard' | 'expert',\n+  local: LatencyProfile,\n+  remote: LatencyProfile,\n+  remoteOverheadMs: number = 0\n+): RouteDecision {\n+  const adjustedRemote = {\n+    ...remote,\n+    meanMs: remote.meanMs + remoteOverheadMs,\n+    p95Ms: remote.p95Ms + remoteOverheadMs,\n+  };\n+  const preferred = compareLatencyProfiles(local, adjustedRemote);\n+  const expectedLatencyMs = preferred === 'local' ? local.p95Ms : adjustedRemote.p95Ms;\n+\n+  if (difficulty === 'easy' || difficulty === 'medium') {\n+    return {\n+      provider: 'local',\n+      reason: 'low-difficulty tasks favor local execution',\n+      expectedLatencyMs: local.p95Ms,\n+    };\n+  }\n+  return { provider: preferred, reason: `latency-optimized ${preferred} provider`, expectedLatencyMs };\n+}\n"
      }
    }
  ],
  "plan": [
    "Inspect router decisions API by reading router.ts to understand the current createRouter entry point and identify extension points for difficulty-aware routing.",
    "Compare local vs remote latency profiles by defining a LatencyProfile interface and implementing compareLatencyProfiles that prioritizes p95 latency, then mean latency, to choose the faster provider.",
    "Validate schema for difficultyRouting by validating a JSON schema with required fields (difficultyLevel, route, estimatedLatency, provider), enum constraints, and additionalProperties false.",
    "Apply patch to router.ts to add LatencyProfile, RouteDecision, compareLatencyProfiles, and decideDifficultyRoute helpers that route easy/medium tasks locally and optimize hard/expert tasks by latency.",
    "Recommend routing strategy improvements such as dynamic latency telemetry updates and cost-aware thresholds to decide when remote compute overhead is justified."
  ],
  "patch_summary": "The patch extends router.ts with two new interfaces—LatencyProfile and RouteDecision—and two exported functions. compareLatencyProfiles selects the provider with lower p95 latency (falling back to mean latency), while decideDifficultyRoute forces easy/medium tasks to run locally and routes hard/expert tasks to the latency-optimized provider after applying a configurable remote overhead. This makes the router's difficultyRouting decisions explicit, testable, and schema-validatable.",
  "strategy_improvements": [
    "Integrate dynamic latency telemetry so the router recomputes latency profiles from real request traces rather than static values, enabling adaptive routing as load and network conditions change.",
    "Add cost-aware and capability-aware thresholds so remote routing is only chosen when the expected latency reduction or required compute capability exceeds the remote overhead and monetary cost."
  ]
}

